# Tests are opt-in

Mirrors `rules/testing.md` from the EngineOS constitution (this repo's
`CLAUDE.md`) for Cursor sessions. Cursor has no hook system, so the Stop-gate
enforcement that Claude Code gets (`hooks/stop-verify.sh`) does not exist here —
this rule is prompt-only.

## Rule

**The default is NO tests.** Do not author tests and do not run a test suite.
Test work is real work: it gets requested and scoped like any other task, never
smuggled into every change.

**Tests are ON for a task only when one of these holds:**

- The user asks — "write tests", "add coverage", "integration tests for X",
  "E2E", "TDD this", "run the suite".
- The project's own `CLAUDE.md` requires tests for the area being touched
  (project conventions beat these defaults).
- A test-writing task was delegated on purpose.
- The user named a release/merge gate that includes tests. A store submission
  or production release counts.

**Otherwise: write no tests, run no suite.** State the omission in one line so
it is never silent:

`[tests] skipped — not requested`

## Verification timing

- The finalization gate is **lint + typecheck**, run ONCE, after the last unit
  of work is integrated, with output shown.
- Tests join that gate ONLY when tests were ON per the section above. Then they
  run once, at the same moment.
- Never mid-task: no test or typecheck run per edit, per file, or per
  intermediate step. Write freely; verify at the end.
- Narrowing the gate makes what remains MORE mandatory, not optional. Red means
  a fix loop until green, with output shown.

## Hard limits

- DON'T author "just a couple of quick tests" beside a feature nobody asked to
  test, and don't scaffold a test file "for later".
- DON'T run the suite to "check nothing broke". Lint, typecheck, and the user's
  own review carry that load by default.
- DON'T delete, skip, `.only`, or weaken EXISTING tests to make a gate pass.
  Code you didn't touch keeps its tests. If a change genuinely invalidates a
  test, say so and ask — never silently neutralize it.
- Bug fixes: a regression test is RECOMMENDED, not automatic. Offer it in one
  line ("this fix ships without a regression test — want one?") and move on
  unless the user takes it up.
- When in doubt, ask before writing tests — never write them and ask after.

## Why this exists

Reflexive test authoring and suite runs were the main thing stalling the build
loop. In Claude Code the Stop hook enforces the narrowed gate and honours
`ENGINEOS_VERIFY_TESTS=1` for teams that want tests back in unconditionally.
Cursor has no equivalent hook point, so this file is best-effort: it only works
if the model reads and follows it. Full policy, including the craft guidance
that applies once tests ARE on: `rules/testing.md`.
